<title>FRANCE: EP backs new EU states' accession to Lome accord.</title>
<headline>EP backs new EU states' accession to Lome accord.</headline>
<dateline>STRASBOURG 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austria, Finland and Sweden on Thursday formally joined the Lome Convention, the European Union's trade and aid pact with 70 developing countries in Africa, the Caribbean and the Pacific (ACP).</p>
<p>The three new EU member states' accession to the Lome Convention formally came into effect after the European Parliament signalled its approval on Thursday.</p>
<p>The Convention has provided EU aid and preferential trading terms to the ACP states, many of which are former European colonies, for the last 20 years.</p>
<p>It expires in its current form in the year 2000 and many ACP countries fear it will not be renewed.</p>
</text>
